Whittier, Alaska (test fragment, How It's Run) · third-party data, assets and tools

Map data and imagery (downloaded by tools/*.py; every URL and date in raw/manifest.jsonl)
- Imagery: Sentinel-2 cloudless 2016 - https://s2maps.eu by EOX IT Services GmbH (Contains modified Copernicus Sentinel data 2016 & 2017), CC BY 4.0. Layer s2cloudless_3857 (the 2016 release): zoom 13 (Whittier), zoom 11 (Anchorage–Prince William Sound), zoom 7 (Alaska, on the globe), zoom 4 (whole globe).
- Elevation: AWS Terrain Tiles (Mapzen/Tilezen "terrarium"), https://registry.opendata.aws/terrain-tiles/ , zoom 12 and 10. Sources include SRTM, GMTED, ETOPO1, GEBCO and USGS 3DEP; attribution as required by the terrain-tiles documentation. Vertical exaggeration ×2.
- Coastline, Begich Towers position, Anton Anderson Memorial Tunnel geometry: © OpenStreetMap contributors, Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0, via the Overpass API (maps.mail.ru mirror) and Nominatim.
- The road from Anchorage is schematic; the sea's depth shading is schematic (distance from shore), not measured bathymetry.
- The film carries a credit line in the bottom-right corner throughout.

Facts: FACTS.md (Alaska Public Media 2013, 2021; Alaska Public Media / Alaska Beacon 2025).

Voice: Kokoro-82M (hexgrad), voice am_puck, speed 1.05, Apache License 2.0, run locally via kokoro-onnx (MIT). Speech check: faster-whisper small.en (MIT).

Fonts: Barlow Condensed (Jeremy Tribby), SIL Open Font License 1.1 (fonts/OFL-barlow.txt).

Music and sound: synthesized in mix.py (numpy/scipy) and with the procedural foley of the Lemo-Opuscar library (core/audio/sfx.py, MIT). No samples.

Engine: built with the Lemo-Opuscar library (3D Map Explainer style; code MIT), three.js (MIT).
